    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Building Reusable Prompts with CHAT, Part 4\r\n\r\n**Context:** You have successfully built a \"Warming Center Finder.\" But next week, you might need to build a \"Music Playlist\" or a \"Recipe Book.\" The code pattern (_an array of objects rendered to a list_) is the same!\r\n\r\n**The 'T' in CHAT is Transfer.**\r\nUse the computational thinking skill of **_abstraction_** to turn your specific \"Warming Center\" prompt into a general tool you can reuse in other contexts.\r\n\r\n1.  **Generalize**: Rewrite your prompt from Level 2/3.\r\n    * Replace \"Warming Center\" with `[MY_TOPIC]`.\r\n    * Replace specific fields like \"capacity\" with `[MY_FIELDS]`.\r\n    * Replace specific IDs like \"#list\" with `[CONTAINER_ID]`.\r\n3.  **Save to Backpack**: Ensure your new prompt explains *how* to process the data (using `.map()`) without being tied to specific data.\r\n",
